  "scientific_findings": [
    "The compact recurrent visual arm beats the task/action control by 0.02074962797619051 regret and its paired upper bound is just below zero, but it misses the absolute 0.13 regret gate.",
    "The parameter-matched no-vision arm is better than the visual arm by 0.007486979166666657 regret. The visual-minus-no-vision interval crosses zero and has a positive upper bound, so incremental visual value is not established.",
    "The no-vision arm beats task/action by 0.028236607142857167 regret with a wholly negative paired interval. The established gain is attributable to executed odometry/action history rather than visual evidence.",
    "The visual arm also has worse scene-disjoint standardized physical MSE than no-vision, 0.8001208879799897 versus 0.7760643819338865, consistent with the branch-selection result rather than an objective/scorer reversal.",
    "This is a valid development-only stop result, not evidence for closed-loop planning, navigation, a final world model, or a blind rollout promotion."
  ],
